hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"307","We are Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar, we are Muhammad bin Jaafar, Shu`bah told us. H Muhammad bin Bashar, narrated to us Abu Amir, narrated to us Qurrah all of us, on the authority of Abu Jamrat al-Dhabi’i, who is Nasr bin Imran, said: I said to Ibn Abbas “I have a pitcher in which I retreat, and I drink from it. If I sit for a long time with the people, I fear that I will be exposed to its sweetness.” He said: A delegation presented Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Welcome the delegation, without shame or regret.” They said: O Messenger of God, we are among us. And the polytheists are free from harm among you, and we do not reach you except during the sacred months. So tell us a sentence of the matter if we take it and act upon it, or if One of us did it, and he entered Paradise with it, and we invite to it those behind us. He said: “I command you to do four things, and I forbid you to do four things: belief in God, and... Do you know what faith in God is? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: Bearing witness that there is no god but God, establishing prayer, paying zakat, and fasting. Ramadan, and you shall be given one-fifth of the spoils, and I forbid you from drinking wine in the form of dhabba, an-naqir, hantam, and mixed-mixtures.” This is the wording of the hadith of Qurrah bin Khalid"
